  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience through Asset Creation and Enhancement (Evaluation)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience through Asset Creation and Enhancement &#x2013; Phase II (BRACE II) was a resilience and international climate finance programme that lasted from 2015 to 2023, funded by the United Kingdom&#x2019;s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO). The programme sought to increase the capacity of vulnerable households to cope with climate shocks and stresses, improve their food security and build better community relationships. This evaluation contract aimed to generate insights and lessons on programme effectiveness and sustainability as well as provide recommendations for future iterations.</narrative>
  </description>
